s($,"aWu","aFX",()=>{var q=t.s
return A.b([A.Ko("Out of Bounds","**What is Out of Bounds?**\n\nOut of bounds is any area outside the course boundary, usually marked by white stakes or a fence line. A ball is out of bounds only if the entire ball lies out of bounds.\n\n**The Procedure**\n\nWhen your ball is out of bounds, you must proceed under stroke and distance:\n\n- Return to the spot of your previous stroke (or as near as possible)\n- Add one penalty stroke to your score\n- Play a ball from that spot\n\n**Example:** You play your tee shot and it crosses the white stakes. You must re-tee, hitting your third shot with a one-stroke penalty.","r1",1,"18.2","Ball OOB? Return to original spot and add one penalty stroke.",A.b(["Stroke & Distance","Penalty"],q),"Stroke and Distance Relief"),A.Ko("Penalty Areas","**Red Penalty Areas (red stakes/lines)**\n\nA red penalty area gives you three options, all with a one-stroke penalty:\n\n- **Option 1 \u2014 Stroke and Distance:** Play again from where you played your last stroke.\n- **Option 2 \u2014 Back-on-the-Line Relief:** Drop on the line going back from the hole.\n- **Option 3 \u2014 Lateral Relief:** Drop within two club-lengths of the crossing point.\n\n**Yellow Penalty Areas**\n\nYellow areas only allow Options 1 and 2 \u2014 no lateral relief.","r2",1,"17.1d","Red penalty areas give three relief options with one penalty stroke.",A.b(["Penalty Area","Lateral Relief"],q),"Taking Relief from a Red Penalty Area"),A.Ko("Unplayable Ball","**When to Use**\n\nYou are the sole judge of whether your ball is unplayable. You may declare it unplayable anywhere on the course except in a penalty area.\n\n**The Three Relief Options (all add one penalty stroke):**\n\n- **Option 1 \u2014 Stroke and Distance:** Return to where you played your last stroke.\n- **Option 2 \u2014 Back-on-the-Line:** Drop on the line from the hole through the ball.\n- **Option 3 \u2014 Two Club-Length Lateral Relief:** Drop within two club-lengths.\n\n**In a Bunker**\n\nIf your ball is unplayable in a bunker, Options 1 and 3 require the ball to be dropped inside the bunker. Option 2 may be taken outside for two strokes.","r3",1,"19.2","Declare any ball unplayable anywhere (except penalty areas) for one stroke.",A.b(["Unplayable","Relief"],q),"Three Options for an Unplayable Ball"),A.Ko("Scorecard Etiquette","**Responsibilities**\n\nBoth the player and the marker share responsibility for the scorecard.\n\n**The Rules**\n\n- The player is responsible for the correctness of the score for each hole\n- The marker must certify the scorecard by signing or initialling it\n- A wrong score lower than actual = **disqualification**\n- A wrong score higher than actual = the higher score stands\n\n**Best Practice**\n\nKeep a running tally during the round and agree scores verbally with your marker at the end of each hole before signing and submitting.","r4",1,"3.3b","Each hole score must be correct and certified before submission.",A.b(["Scorecard","Etiquette"],q),"Completing and Certifying Your Scorecard"),A.Ko("Local Rules","**When It Applies**\n\nDuring Trinidad and Tobago's wet season (June\u2013November), many clubs adopt a Local Rule allowing preferred lies through the green.\n\n**The Procedure**\n\n- Mark your ball position\n- Lift, clean, and place the ball within one scorecard length (no nearer the hole)\n- The ball must be placed on a closely mown area\n\n**Check Your Club's Local Rules**\n\nAlways check the notice board at the first tee or ask the pro shop before your round whether preferred lies are in operation.","r5",1,"Local","Many Caribbean clubs allow preferred lies during wet season.",A.b(["Local Rules","Caribbean","Wet Season"],q),"Caribbean Preferred Lies (Lift, Clean & Place)")],t.AS)})
